// The smallest complete Jux program: an entry point and one line of output.
// `jux run` in this directory builds the project and executes the result.

// `main` is where every executable package starts. A free `main` needs no
// `public` or `static` (Entry Points §E.1.2); returning `void` means the
// process exits with status zero.
void main() {
    // `print` writes the text and ends the line, so no "\n" is needed.
    print("Hello, World!");
}
